# Functions are documented before their release. At release, remove these
# entries, add the pages back to the navigation in docs.json (chunking.mdx
# goes back into the Curation group, and curation/index.mdx's "Chunk records"
# row comes back), restore the /feature-engineering/functions redirect to
# /management/function, publish the drafts marked "Draft for the Functions
# release", and restore `availability` frontmatter (removed while gated,
# since the comparison table on index.mdx links every page that declares
# one, draft or not) to management/function.mdx, sql/ddl/function.mdx and
# curation/chunking.mdx -- each currently carries a plain
# `<Badge color="red">Enterprise</Badge>` instead. Chunking depends on
# Functions (it runs one in the FROM clause to explode rows), so it is gated
# with them rather than publishing a guide for SQL that does not run yet.
management/function.mdx
sql/ddl/function.mdx
curation/chunking.mdx

# GRANT/REVOKE currently only covers privileges on Secrets and Functions
# (CREATE SECRET, CREATE FUNCTION, USAGE on a secret or function), which are
# themselves part of the Functions release: see the "Draft for the Functions
# release" block in governance/authorization.mdx#privileges. At release,
# remove this entry, add the page to the navigation in docs.json, and give it
# `availability` frontmatter like the rest of the SQL reference.
sql/ddl/grant.mdx
